WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.230
Shame! Shame! Shame!

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.380
Lots of people hate Education Secretary

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.740
Betsy DeVos.

00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:11.110
What’s her response to the haters?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.400
It's really disappointing and disturbing.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.930
When she spoke at the Kennedy School of  Government,

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.044
students held up signs calling her a

00:00:19.044 --> 00:00:20.280
white supremacist,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.940
and saying “students are not for sale".

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.120
Our kids are not for sale.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.210
Of course they’re not.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.446
The Secretary tries to get in the back door of the school

00:00:27.446 --> 00:00:31.289
but she is confronted physically

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.720
and then blocked out.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.007
Right after she took office,

00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:36.260
she went to visit this school but

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.310
protesters blocked her way.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.329
I am undeterred.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:40.540
You are undeterred?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.960
You're being turned away from the school.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.760
Go back!

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.940
The security person had me get back in
the car.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.220
We drove away and he said

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.370
"Ma'am, I don't think we should go back there."

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.050
And I said "We are absolutely going back there.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.020
You're going to figure out a way to get me in,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.920
because they are not going to win."

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.080
And you got back in that school.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.040
I got back in, and I had a great visit.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.110
Some people hate DeVos because

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:04.640
she's a rich Republican donor.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.860
Betsy DeVos is a billionaire,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.290
she was born into a billionaire family…

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.670
She is rich.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.540
Her father built a company worth more than

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.915
a billion dollars.

00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:19.110
Then she married into

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.170
to the Amway marketing fortune.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.880
Betsy DeVos’ primary expertise

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.060
seems to be in being a rich person.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.160
Buying your way into the position.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.570
Ridiculous.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:31.260
Well you did give a lot of money

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.090
to some Republican senators.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.560
Yes, I have been a contributor over the years.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.409
I've also been an activist over the years.

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:39.540
I think it's important for people to engage

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.840
in things that they believe in.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.030
But that's not the point.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.620
The point is for 30 years I have been working

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.380
on behalf of families that have not had opportunity.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.520
For 30 years, she’s obsessed about

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.920
giving poor families a chance to attend better schools.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.520
She donated million of dollars to charter schools

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.060
and private schools, and served on the boards

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.740
of school choice foundations.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.060
That enrages the education establishment.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.869
What she has done is actually made schooling

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:11.510
worse in Michigan.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.060
DeVos helped bring charter schools to Michigan,

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.260
and the union boss claims:

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.280
80 percent of the  schools,

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.830
the charter schools in Detroit are

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.620
failing.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.520
Charters in Detroit are at the bottom of the list.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.100
Charter schools in Michigan actually,

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.460
the students in them are doing demonstrably

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:33.690
better than the students in traditional public schools.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.560
And that goes for the city of Detroit and statewide.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.940
She’s right.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.460
Stanford researchers found

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.940
the kids in charters performed better.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.500
Choice did help.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.183
The whole country could use help.

00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:49.660
You look at our standing vis a vis

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.061
the rest of the world,

00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:53.921
it has been stagnant for the last 30 years.

00:02:53.921 --> 00:02:55.180
23rd in reading,

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.840
25th in science,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.760
40th in math.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.180
And we've tripled spending on K-12 education.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.900
But we haven't gotten the results that we've hoped for

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.100
and expected.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:06.980
Why not?

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.340
The reality is today,

00:03:08.342 --> 00:03:12.300
almost all the schools that kids go to are still

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.620
operating on the industrial model.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:17.930
Why do we group kids by age in school?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.920
Why do we take the summer off?

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.220
Because that's the way it was always done.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.120
Most of it is based on history

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.120
and tradition.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.620
Kids get the summer off

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.310
because they're needed on the farm.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.891
A hundred years ago when most worked on the farm.

00:03:32.891 --> 00:03:34.460
A hundred years ago, yes.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.260
If we were to introduce

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.960
full on choice

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.560
into an education environment,

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.440
you're going to have a lot of

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.907
different approaches.

00:03:43.907 --> 00:03:45.580
If there were real choice,

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.470
good teachers would make

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.819
more money.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:49.819
Absolutely.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:50.600
Good teachers

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.140
should be very handsomely compensated.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.879
By the same token, teachers

00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:58.661
who aren't good and really shouldn't be in the classroom

00:03:58.661 --> 00:04:00.620
probably wouldn't be anymore

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.739
because nobody would choose their classroom.

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:04.127
People are not stupid,

00:04:04.127 --> 00:04:07.040
they know where their kid is gonna do best.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.180
I knew which teacher I wanted my child to have.

00:04:10.188 --> 00:04:12.610
We need to do something different.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:18.220
This country is on a trajectory to failure,

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.880
ultimately, if we do not turn around how

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:23.419
we are educating kids today.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.160
DeVos also acknowledges that

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.560
fixing schools

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.280
is not her job,

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.940
not the federal government's job.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:34.080
Most schools are locally controlled, and paid for locally.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.360
DeVos, less arrogant than many in Washington,

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.640
told me "I'm not

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.199
the nation's choice chief".

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:42.389
All she can do is encourage states

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:43.320
and local governments to

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.380
try choice,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.120
and to get rid of rules that get in the way.

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:49.101
President Trump signed an Executive Order

00:04:49.101 --> 00:04:50.520
directing her to

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.700
do that.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.200
As The President said:

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.599
"Local communities do it best and know

00:04:55.599 --> 00:04:56.599
it best.”

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.900
That’s usually true.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.520
Local control has its advantages.

